sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/flying-fish-glides-at-or-above-minimum-lift-speed> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "A flying fish glides at or above the slowest speed its fins can hold it up at" ;
    dct:description "From the measured weight (0.5886 N), reference lifting area (0.01269 m2) and maximum lift coefficient (0.78) of a darkedged-wing flying fish specimen (Park and Choi 2010, model L3), the slowest lift-supported speed is v_min = sqrt(2W/(rho S C_Lmax)) = 9.85 m/s at rho = 1.225 kg/m3. Published field glide speeds for flying fish are 10 to 20 m/s (Hertel 1966, Fish 1990, Davenport 1994, as quoted by Park and Choi 2010 and Makiguchi et al. 2013). The quoted speeds overlap the pre-registered band [v_min, 3 v_min] = [9.85, 29.56] m/s, so under this reading the fish is inside Thompson's envelope: supported." ;
    delphi:context "Claim under test: thompson1917-ch02-06 (D Arcy Thompson 1917, On Growth and Form, ch. II, Project Gutenberg 55264 lines 1716-1790), with thompson1917-ch02-07 and thompson1917-ch02-10. Taxon: Exocoetidae, NCBI Taxonomy 76072, GBIF 2968. Class Aves is the frozen holdout (holdout/exam.json); no bird value enters this record." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-thompson-ch02-06-reading-B> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.046052>, <https://doi.org/10.3354/ab00494>, <https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-3190/ab23e6> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: sea-level air density 1.225 kg/m3; steady lift-supported flight with lift equal to weight; C_Lmax from a stuffed specimen at 12 m/s applies in free flight." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Measured: W, S, C_Lmax (Park and Choi 2010). Secondary: the field airspeed range. Simulation excluded: Deng 2019 CFD values enter no verdict." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: supported. Does not establish: that the glide speeds were measured on the fish whose wing loading was measured (the speeds are family-level, second-hand figures for larger fish of several genera; the morphometrics are 40 to 60 g stuffed specimens of one species, a weakness the pre-registration did not foresee and that is recorded there as a caveat); that C_Lmax is the same in free flight as in the wind tunnel; anything about Thompson's scaling law across sizes (that is reading A, inconclusive); anything about birds." ;
    rdfs:comment "Pre-registration: physics/tests/thompson1917-ch02-06/result.json, written 2026-10-31T18:21:00Z before any wing loading, lifting area or lift coefficient was read, amended 2026-10-31T18:26:00Z before any fit ran (the file lists both and the values seen before each); sha256 at build 0094c084db22278a5f98d96cc2971ccd27813b0acdc458d60cadf7c7b7bcae48. The git commit that timestamps it is pending: the physics thread does not commit; the hub does." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-thompson-ch02-06-reading-B> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Computation of v_min for Cypselurus hiraii specimen L3 and comparison with quoted field glide speeds" ;
    dct:description "Inputs: body mass 0.06 kg, pectoral fin area 6377 mm2, pelvic fin area 1837 mm2, body planform 4474 mm2, C_Lmax 0.78 at 35 deg attack (Park and Choi 2010, J Exp Biol 213:3269, Tables 1 and 2, full text retrieved 2026-10-31T18:18:51Z); airspeed 10 to 20 m/s (Park and Choi 2010 introduction quoting Hertel 1966, Fish 1990, Davenport 1994; Makiguchi et al. 2013 introduction quoting Edgerton and Breder 1941 and Davenport 1990). Result: wing loading 46.4 N/m2, v_min 9.85 m/s, band to 29.56 m/s, verdict inside. Second specimen, descriptive only: Cheilopogon heterurus doederleini 0.226 kg over 0.0225 m2 (Kawachi et al. 1993 as quoted by Deng et al. 2019) gives 98.5 N/m2 and v_min 14.4 m/s with the borrowed C_Lmax." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/flying-fish-glides-at-or-above-minimum-lift-speed> ;
    rdfs:comment "Computed by physics/analysis.py from physics/glide-data.csv (sha256 bc24245b5163723b192e95fccf714ef6e4b3b28e71df4fef3befbaf008a00635) and physics/comparison-data.csv (sha256 e0d3d74639c1fe856fe5128c1783151596fde3acc923a2409be3d3f870cc394a); numbers in physics/results.json (sha256 63336841c0d4c9ae2760ae5c87a9251b97218e3ebfdd453cad4cffb9cdf6ba0b). Every input value carries its source, locator, retrieval time and value kind in those files." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/glide-data.csv>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/comparison-data.csv> .
}

